WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.842
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:07.112 --> 00:09.114
[theme music playing]

3
00:33.764 --> 00:36.642
[banging on door]

4
00:36.725 --> 00:38.602
Open the door!

5
00:39.144 --> 00:40.729
I said open it!

6
00:40.813 --> 00:43.399
[sobs] Come on. Open up.

7
00:44.233 --> 00:45.943
Please open!

8
00:46.652 --> 00:48.571
Please open the door!

9
00:49.572 --> 00:51.615
Dad, please!

10
00:51.699 --> 00:54.410
[crying, breathing shakily]

11
00:57.746 --> 00:59.540
[mysterious music playing]

12
01:05.713 --> 01:07.464
[gentle music playing]

13
01:22.354 --> 01:25.065
[intense music playing]

14
01:25.149 --> 01:26.775
[glass shattering]

15
01:29.486 --> 01:30.988
-[grunting] -[grunting]

16
01:34.450 --> 01:35.618
Push, damn it!

17
01:37.077 --> 01:38.370
Find him!

18
01:49.298 --> 01:50.549
[alarm blaring]

19
02:11.904 --> 02:13.322
[alarm blaring continues]

20
02:23.499 --> 02:24.500
[panting]

21
02:38.389 --> 02:40.224
[intense music playing]

22
02:42.810 --> 02:43.811
[panting]

23
02:53.112 --> 02:54.196
Ow!

24
03:19.096 --> 03:21.598
[San] Son. It's time to get up.

25
03:22.349 --> 03:23.350
Son?

26
03:28.397 --> 03:29.398
Hurry. Wake up.

27
03:30.691 --> 03:32.151
It's not time yet.

28
03:32.985 --> 03:33.986
Not yet.

29
03:36.321 --> 03:38.365
Get up. Get up, Son.

30
03:39.700 --> 03:40.743
-Wake up! -[gasps]

31
03:44.913 --> 03:45.914
[breathing heavily]

32
04:11.190 --> 04:13.484
[intense music playing]

33
04:14.193 --> 04:15.944
[gunshot]

34
04:19.364 --> 04:20.699
[panting]

35
04:28.332 --> 04:29.333
Oh, damn it!

36
04:30.042 --> 04:31.335
-[yelps] -[snorting]

37
04:43.222 --> 04:45.516
[snorting continues]

38
04:46.475 --> 04:49.728
[gasps, yelps]

39
04:49.812 --> 04:50.813
[snorts]

40
04:55.984 --> 04:58.028
[gasps, groaning]

41
05:01.782 --> 05:04.159
-[gasps, screams] -[gunshot]

42
05:17.464 --> 05:19.633
[gasps, panting]

43
05:41.905 --> 05:43.657
Gosh. [panting]

44
05:43.740 --> 05:44.825
Th-Thank you.

45
05:45.576 --> 05:47.202
But who…

46
05:56.086 --> 05:57.129
Who are you?

47
06:10.058 --> 06:11.310
-[gasps, screams] -[squeals]

48
06:28.994 --> 06:29.995
[sighs]

49
06:33.957 --> 06:36.210
[rock music playing]

50
06:39.379 --> 06:40.380
[chuckles]

51
06:51.016 --> 06:53.727
-[villager] That's amazing. -[villagers exclaiming]

52
06:53.810 --> 06:55.437
[chattering]

53
07:04.613 --> 07:06.865
[Han] I'm a wizard when it comes to the kitchen.

54
07:44.194 --> 07:46.905
A wizard has no rules to follow.

55
07:47.906 --> 07:49.741
Only the laws of nature.

56
07:54.496 --> 07:56.456
I operate within those laws.

57
07:58.542 --> 07:59.960
Sometimes breaking them…

58
08:02.754 --> 08:04.423
as I create works

59
08:04.923 --> 08:05.924
of my own.

60
08:11.847 --> 08:13.974
The place where I stand is a battlefield.

61
08:14.850 --> 08:17.352
A battlefield filled with fire and smoke,

62
08:17.978 --> 08:19.688
but with no shell fire.

63
08:28.947 --> 08:31.325
[villagers exclaiming, chattering]

64
08:31.408 --> 08:35.412
I am an actor standing before an audience.

65
08:36.121 --> 08:37.414
But I'm also the writer

66
08:38.415 --> 08:42.044
and the director who is responsible for it all.

67
08:44.087 --> 08:46.423
[upbeat music playing]

68
08:51.303 --> 08:52.346
[exhales]

69
08:52.429 --> 08:54.139
[villagers exclaiming, chattering]

70
08:58.101 --> 08:59.102
[huffs]

71
08:59.895 --> 09:03.565
Cooking isn't just about making people happy.

72
09:04.358 --> 09:05.776
[chattering, laughing]

73
09:08.612 --> 09:10.280
And it smells so delicious.

74
09:10.364 --> 09:11.365
Wow, you're here.

75
09:11.448 --> 09:12.949
[chattering continues]

76
09:16.203 --> 09:21.208
[Han] Cooking is about the joy I feel when I cook for others.

77
09:25.045 --> 09:26.463
I am

78
09:26.546 --> 09:28.006
a chef.

79
09:33.762 --> 09:36.056
[gentle music playing]

80
09:49.069 --> 09:50.070
[huffs]

81
09:51.071 --> 09:52.531
[sighs deeply]

82
09:58.870 --> 09:59.871
[sighs]

83
10:01.456 --> 10:02.999
FAMIGLIA CHEF CHOI SEUNG-HYO

84
10:03.083 --> 10:07.796
1ST-GEN ITALIAN STAR CHEF CHOI, A DECLARATION OF LIES?

85
10:07.879 --> 10:10.340
1ST-GEN STAR CHEF, A MAN OF PRINCIPLE…

86
10:24.104 --> 10:25.147
Auntie.

87
10:27.482 --> 10:28.567
[sighs]

88
10:37.617 --> 10:38.869
Oh. Hello.

89
10:39.995 --> 10:41.663
You must be exhausted.

90
10:41.746 --> 10:44.166
Good work, everyone. Go on home now.

91
10:44.249 --> 10:46.168
You can go on ahead, Dad.

92
10:46.251 --> 10:47.961
We'll stay so we can clean up a bit.

93
10:48.044 --> 10:51.173
Well, I mean, what's there to clean anyway?

94
10:56.970 --> 10:58.430
[footsteps approaching]

95
11:08.815 --> 11:10.442
LETTER OF RESIGNATION

96
11:13.612 --> 11:15.447
I'm really sorry, Chef.

97
11:22.037 --> 11:25.874
[exhales sharply] I shouldn't be doing this at a time like this.

98
11:28.084 --> 11:31.004
-I thought long and hard about it too. -Come on, Chef…

99
11:32.464 --> 11:34.174
[clicks tongue, sighs]

100
11:35.759 --> 11:38.512
[exhales heavily] Thank you so much for everything.

101
11:39.137 --> 11:40.972
I'll never forget your kindness.

102
11:43.517 --> 11:44.518
Take care…

103
11:45.060 --> 11:46.061
everyone.

104
11:49.356 --> 11:50.941
Do you have somewhere to be?

105
11:54.402 --> 11:56.988
Do you have another job lined up?

106
12:03.245 --> 12:05.247
[smacks lips, inhales sharply]

107
12:06.206 --> 12:08.583
-I'm going to La Fleur at the PL Hotel. -[gasps]

108
12:12.587 --> 12:14.297
-What? -Yes.

109
12:15.590 --> 12:16.591
The PL Hotel.

110
12:17.968 --> 12:19.636
Pyeongyeon Group's PL Hotel.

111
12:24.432 --> 12:25.517
Look, I know, Chef.

112
12:26.768 --> 12:28.270
Pyeongyeon Group is corrupt

113
12:28.937 --> 12:31.147
and Plate In Asia is totally rigged.

114
12:31.731 --> 12:32.732
But…

115
12:36.027 --> 12:38.071
I'm doing what I can to survive.

116
12:39.197 --> 12:40.198
Because

117
12:41.449 --> 12:42.742
we just can't beat those guys.

118
12:47.622 --> 12:49.207
[sighs] I'm sorry.

119
12:49.791 --> 12:52.252
Thank you, all, for everything you've done.

120
12:58.592 --> 13:00.260
[door closes]

121
13:01.219 --> 13:02.387
[chuckles]

122
13:32.417 --> 13:35.128
[sighs] Well, then, good for him.

123
13:35.795 --> 13:38.298
[exhales deeply] Lucky bastard. [clicks tongue]

124
13:38.381 --> 13:39.716
I wish I could go with him.

125
13:39.799 --> 13:42.927
Of course I had to apply to Famiglia at the worst possible time.

126
13:43.595 --> 13:46.765
[sighs deeply] Yeah, talk about rotten luck. [smacks lips]

127
13:46.848 --> 13:47.849
"If you'll just have me, Chef,

128
13:47.932 --> 13:50.935
I promise I'll grind my own flesh and bones into puree if I have to."

129
13:56.608 --> 13:59.444
That's what you said to my dad the day you came for your interview.

130
14:00.445 --> 14:01.446
[sighs]

131
14:02.238 --> 14:03.239
Well…

132
14:03.865 --> 14:08.620
you know, I'd been rejected so many times, it just slipped out. [chuckles]

133
14:17.212 --> 14:18.672
Hey, wait…

134
14:23.635 --> 14:25.679
FAMIGLIA RESERVATION PORTAL

135
14:25.762 --> 14:27.055
JOIN THE FAMILY

136
14:28.556 --> 14:29.891
2 JOB OPENINGS

137
14:29.974 --> 14:32.060
0 APPLICANTS

138
14:34.270 --> 14:35.480
[clears throat]

139
14:37.399 --> 14:39.442
SOUS CHEF WANTED

140
14:39.526 --> 14:41.277
[announcer on TV] Plate In Asia was a system created

141
14:41.361 --> 14:43.863
to establish a proper food evaluation standard

142
14:43.947 --> 14:47.575
tailored specifically to kitchens that served exclusively Asian cuisine.

143
14:47.659 --> 14:51.204
The controversy began when Famiglia's head chef Choi Seung-hyo

144
14:51.287 --> 14:53.998
publicly criticized the Plate In Asia system.

145
14:54.082 --> 14:57.335
Chef Choi claims that some chefs lobbied Pyeongyeon

146
14:57.419 --> 14:59.045
in order to receive Plates,

147
14:59.129 --> 15:02.799
while chefs who aren't favorable toward Pyeongyeon are pushed out.

148
15:02.882 --> 15:06.886
Ultimately, what Chef Choi is claiming is that Plate In Asia is muddying the waters

149
15:06.970 --> 15:08.513
of the restaurant industry.

150
15:08.596 --> 15:09.681
So we'd like to ask

151
15:09.764 --> 15:12.642
how does Pyeongyeon Group respond to these allegations?

152
15:12.726 --> 15:15.103
[Pyeongyeon representative] Unfortunately, we can't idly sit by anymore.

153
15:15.186 --> 15:19.649
We feel that pursuing legal action is unavoidable at this point.

154
15:19.733 --> 15:21.359
ANONYMOUS FORUM

155
15:21.443 --> 15:22.902
THAT HAPPENED TO MY ACQUAINTANCE

156
15:22.986 --> 15:26.489
[commenter] A friend of mine almost died after eating a meal at Famiglia last week.

157
15:26.573 --> 15:28.241
[commenter 2] Seriously? That's ridiculous.

158
15:28.324 --> 15:29.826
What kind of restaurant is that?

159
15:29.909 --> 15:31.369
If they don't even check the bare basics,

160
15:31.453 --> 15:33.037
of course they should never be awarded a Plate.

161
15:33.121 --> 15:35.623
[commenter 3] If he wanted to turn down a Plate, he should've done it alone.

162
15:35.707 --> 15:37.292
Why threaten other chefs into joining him?

163
15:37.375 --> 15:39.252
Who could say no to an industry vet like him?

164
15:39.335 --> 15:40.670
[commenter 4] You saw last year's article?

165
15:40.754 --> 15:42.088
He says he's about being considerate,

166
15:42.172 --> 15:44.424
right down to that photo of him wearing that fake smile.

167
15:44.507 --> 15:45.925
To think that it was all for show…

168
15:46.009 --> 15:49.596
A former kitchen staff member came forward saying he'd always swear and hit people.

169
15:49.679 --> 15:50.889
That's scary.

170
15:50.972 --> 15:53.516
[host] How can someone be so two-faced?

171
15:53.600 --> 15:55.310
What I heard of Choi Seung-hyo

172
15:55.393 --> 15:58.521
was that he was a real thug and routinely threatened his fellow chefs too.

173
15:58.605 --> 16:03.318
From what I understand, he's actually been openly opposing the Plate In Asia system.

174
16:03.401 --> 16:05.403
Actually, if you remember well,

175
16:05.487 --> 16:07.697
he was once quite obsessed with Plate In Asia.

176
16:07.781 --> 16:09.741
He kept trying his luck with Pyeongyeon Group,

177
16:09.824 --> 16:11.618
but when he couldn't get the result he wanted,

178
16:11.701 --> 16:14.204
he turned around and started criticizing the whole system.

179
16:14.287 --> 16:18.249
He instigated the chefs who followed him, pressuring them to return their Plates,

180
16:18.333 --> 16:22.754
even yelling and throwing punches toward those who refused.

181
16:22.837 --> 16:24.547
[commenter] So when it looked like you wouldn't get a Plate,

182
16:24.631 --> 16:26.466
you suddenly decided to reject it?

183
16:26.549 --> 16:29.260
Well, isn't that impressive? That's quite the scenario you cooked up

184
16:29.344 --> 16:31.054
with awfully convenient timing too.

185
16:31.137 --> 16:32.680
But the public isn't that stupid.

186
16:32.764 --> 16:34.974
-Famiglia, you actually disgust me. -[commenter 2] As someone

187
16:35.058 --> 16:37.519
in the restaurant industry myself, I'm ashamed that people like you even exist.

188
16:37.602 --> 16:39.521
[commenter 3] Now everyone is talking about kitchen bullies

189
16:39.604 --> 16:40.647
instead of school bullies?

190
16:40.730 --> 16:42.565
False propaganda, stealing ingredients.

191
16:42.649 --> 16:44.859
Threatening junior chefs, sexual harassment

192
16:44.943 --> 16:45.985
and verbal abuse in the kitchen.

193
16:46.069 --> 16:49.405
Trash like Choi Seung-hyo isn't even worth wasting a trash bag on.

194
16:49.489 --> 16:50.824
You should be ashamed!

195
16:50.907 --> 16:52.659
Aren't you embarrassed to face your daughter?

196
16:56.204 --> 16:58.498
[Song-yi] Excuse me, but on which day did you visit us last week?

197
16:58.581 --> 17:00.959
We didn't even buy apples last week.

198
17:01.042 --> 17:02.335
What apple sauce?

199
17:03.002 --> 17:04.838
The toilet in the women's restroom was clogged?

200
17:04.921 --> 17:07.632
If that's true, why didn't you say anything to the staff?

201
17:07.715 --> 17:10.635
And about Pyeongyeon's Group Plate? It's not that he couldn't get one.

202
17:10.718 --> 17:14.097
He got one, but he refused to accept it. Get your facts straight.

203
17:14.180 --> 17:16.683
He never swore at or hit anyone ever!

204
17:18.351 --> 17:19.352
[sighs]

205
17:21.145 --> 17:23.398
[commenter 5] What's this? Does this person work at Famiglia?

206
17:23.481 --> 17:24.774
[commenter 6] I guess? Certainly sounds like it.

207
17:24.858 --> 17:26.359
[commenter 7] Ugh, must be a Famiglia employee.

208
17:26.442 --> 17:28.194
-So annoying. -[commenter 8] This is ridiculous.

209
17:28.278 --> 17:30.822
[commenter 9] Typical. Losers always have the most excuses.

210
17:33.616 --> 17:35.994
[Song-yi] Yes. I work at Famiglia.

211
17:36.077 --> 17:38.329
And aren't you people just paid shills for Pyeongyeon Group?

212
17:38.413 --> 17:40.623
If you're going to criticize based on facts,

213
17:40.707 --> 17:43.334
shouldn't it be based on what you actually saw and experienced firsthand?

214
17:43.418 --> 17:46.963
Do you have any idea how much every single one of these irresponsible comments

215
17:47.046 --> 17:49.507
hurts the person who's being falsely accused?

216
17:53.261 --> 17:54.262
[sighs]

217
18:04.522 --> 18:05.940
[door opens]

218
18:18.912 --> 18:20.288
[winces]

219
18:31.799 --> 18:34.177
-[knocking quietly] -[Song-yi] Dad.

220
18:40.975 --> 18:42.310
Hey, Dad, are you asleep?

221
18:49.776 --> 18:51.527
Dad, want to have a beer with…

222
18:57.825 --> 18:58.826
[gasps]

223
19:02.080 --> 19:04.040
[mysterious music playing]

224
19:18.137 --> 19:19.931
Yes. Hello?

225
19:21.015 --> 19:22.767
[announcer] We've been informed that early this morning,

226
19:22.850 --> 19:26.270
Famiglia chef Choi Seung-hyo has died by suicide.

227
19:26.938 --> 19:30.233
Chef Choi Seung-hyo was one of Korea's leading celebrity chefs

228
19:30.316 --> 19:34.112
and ran Famiglia for 39 years after its opening in 1987.

229
19:34.612 --> 19:37.407
He accused Pyeongyeon of using Plate In Asia

230
19:37.490 --> 19:40.618
as leverage for years of lobbying and intimidation,

231
19:40.702 --> 19:44.706
presenting detailed testimony and evidence from multiple people.

232
19:44.789 --> 19:47.750
Initially, Chef Choi Seung-hyo was praised for his courage,

233
19:47.834 --> 19:49.502
and backed by favorable public opinion.

234
19:49.585 --> 19:52.588
However, the tide turned against him overnight.

235
19:53.506 --> 19:56.050
Claims that Chef Choi had staged the whole thing emerged,

236
19:56.134 --> 19:57.969
alleging that he knew in advance

237
19:58.052 --> 20:01.431
that Famiglia would fail to receive a Plate in this year's evaluation.

238
20:01.514 --> 20:04.308
Which caused a stir in the restaurant industry.

239
20:04.892 --> 20:06.102
[chef on TV, voice distorted] I was scared.

240
20:06.185 --> 20:08.646
I had no choice but to do what he told me.

241
20:08.730 --> 20:12.608
Defying him would've been like giving up the career that I built.

242
20:13.776 --> 20:16.487
[chef 2] What can powerless people like us actually do?

243
20:16.571 --> 20:20.908
To us in the industry, Chef Choi Seung-hyo was law and order.

244
20:23.286 --> 20:25.496
[announcer] To make matters worse,

245
20:25.580 --> 20:28.624
people also began coming forward claiming that he had physically assaulted

246
20:28.708 --> 20:30.251
and sexually harassed them.

247
20:30.334 --> 20:33.087
Pyeongyeon Group announced that it would take all possible legal action

248
20:33.171 --> 20:34.380
to fight the allegations.

249
20:34.881 --> 20:38.593
Alone and cornered on all sides by the public opinion,

250
20:38.676 --> 20:41.763
the once-prestigious Chef Choi left a cryptic post on social media

251
20:41.846 --> 20:45.016
early this morning before dying by suicide.

252
20:45.099 --> 20:46.934
[tires screeching]

253
20:47.018 --> 20:49.228
Speculations that pressure from Pyeongyeon Group

254
20:49.312 --> 20:50.980
may have led to his death emerged,

255
20:51.064 --> 20:53.816
triggering a wave of criticism against the company.

256
20:53.900 --> 20:56.194
Further testimony and shifts in public opinion

257
20:56.277 --> 20:59.155
are also expected to affect the police investigation.

258
20:59.655 --> 21:02.158
Jung Ui-gyeong reporting for YTS.

259
21:08.372 --> 21:09.373
[sighs]

260
21:13.669 --> 21:14.921
"Silence is golden."

261
21:17.673 --> 21:19.300
Since you all took that lesson to heart,

262
21:20.301 --> 21:22.678
you must be sitting on a gold mine by now.

263
21:25.765 --> 21:27.683
Why isn't anyone saying anything?

264
21:28.851 --> 21:31.062
Situation assessed. Time, none.

265
21:31.145 --> 21:34.273
No solutions in sight, but we have money and manpower.

266
21:34.357 --> 21:36.692
So what is it that we need right now?

267
21:37.610 --> 21:40.488
A corporate bully driving a poor chef to his death.

268
21:40.571 --> 21:43.574
A police investigation plus online outrage

269
21:43.658 --> 21:46.452
when people are already complaining that we control everything as it is.

270
21:46.536 --> 21:49.038
Next thing you know, they'll be boycotting our products!

271
21:49.122 --> 21:51.499
Do you all wanna watch Pyeongyeon Group go under?

272
21:52.416 --> 21:54.752
-Is that what you all want? -[board member sighs]

273
21:56.295 --> 21:58.089
Pyeongyeon F&B.

274
21:58.172 --> 21:59.590
-Pyeongyeon Construction. -Yes.

275
21:59.674 --> 22:01.050
-Pyeongyeon Global. -Yes.

276
22:01.134 --> 22:02.718
-Pyeongyeon Chemical. -Yes.

277
22:02.802 --> 22:04.095
Pyeongyeon Media.

278
22:04.178 --> 22:05.221
-Yes. -Yes.

279
22:07.056 --> 22:08.766
You have three minutes starting right now.

280
22:10.143 --> 22:14.605
I expect each subsidiary to present a viable solution to resolve this crisis.

281
22:15.606 --> 22:18.025
Remember, three minutes, not 30.

282
22:18.109 --> 22:21.571
Creativity isn't something that kicks in just because you have more time.

283
22:30.663 --> 22:32.373
You have two minutes left.

284
22:33.499 --> 22:35.126
It's one or the other.

285
22:36.043 --> 22:38.337
Come up with the answer that satisfies me,

286
22:38.421 --> 22:41.257
or come up with an answer that is very, very creative.

287
22:42.216 --> 22:44.594
In two minutes, I'll decide whether those of you

288
22:44.677 --> 22:46.554
in this room deserve to keep drawing a salary

289
22:47.305 --> 22:49.599
from Pyeongyeon in the years to come.

290
22:59.233 --> 23:00.359
Pyeongyeon Construction.

291
23:01.986 --> 23:03.196
Our view is that

292
23:03.279 --> 23:06.115
we should first wait and see how the police and prosecutors proceed

293
23:06.199 --> 23:07.867
before taking action.

294
23:07.950 --> 23:10.036
It's very difficult to predict how far

295
23:10.119 --> 23:12.205
-this will escalate. At least for now-- -Pyeongyeon Global.

296
23:12.788 --> 23:16.375
We believe that our top priority right now should be to appease Famiglia.

297
23:17.001 --> 23:19.337
I hear the late Chef Choi Seung-Hyo's daughter

298
23:19.420 --> 23:21.297
is the manager over there.

299
23:21.380 --> 23:24.759
Wouldn't it be important to meet with her and offer her some comfort?

300
23:24.842 --> 23:28.221
If we manage to acquire the restaurant at a reasonable price,

301
23:28.304 --> 23:31.599
I believe we can bring this to an amicable conclusion.

302
23:31.682 --> 23:33.100
We at F&B also agree.

303
23:33.184 --> 23:36.562
We could try to persuade them by offering to honor Chef Choi's wishes

304
23:36.646 --> 23:38.773
-and restore the restaurant's reputation-- -"Appease, persuade."

305
23:38.856 --> 23:41.442
I have no time for these laid-back, abstract nouns.

306
23:41.525 --> 23:44.195
Give me a solution built on simple, concrete nouns and verbs.

307
23:44.278 --> 23:46.822
What we need is a solution! A solution!

308
23:54.789 --> 23:55.790
Um, Chairwoman?

309
24:00.503 --> 24:03.047
I may be overstepping, but I'd like to say something.

310
24:06.384 --> 24:07.593
Please go ahead, Ms. Seon.

311
24:08.594 --> 24:09.720
I believe we should…

312
24:12.682 --> 24:14.976
use this crisis as an opportunity to…

313
24:16.310 --> 24:18.062
abolish Plate In Asia for good.

314
24:19.146 --> 24:22.942
[all murmuring]

315
24:23.025 --> 24:25.987
[whispering] Are you crazy? You've lost your mind, haven't you?

316
24:26.862 --> 24:28.114
Go on, speak.

317
24:35.788 --> 24:36.872
We Koreans grow up

318
24:36.956 --> 24:40.459
under relentless competition and evaluation from an early age.

319
24:40.543 --> 24:43.879
At cram schools, at school and even at home.

320
24:43.963 --> 24:45.881
Constantly compared and evaluated.

321
24:46.465 --> 24:48.634
And the method of evaluation is always the same.

322
24:48.718 --> 24:49.719
It's their scores.

323
24:50.386 --> 24:53.306
For us, Plate serves exactly that function.

324
24:53.389 --> 24:56.934
And we're all exhausted from a life of evaluation based on scores.

325
24:57.601 --> 25:00.104
Regardless of how fair the evaluation system may be,

326
25:00.187 --> 25:02.523
people grow tired of this process.

327
25:03.107 --> 25:04.650
So I had an idea.

328
25:04.734 --> 25:08.571
If competition is something we can never eliminate from our society,

329
25:09.113 --> 25:12.158
then why not give it a more compelling purpose?

330
25:12.742 --> 25:16.829
A compelling purpose that highlights the true nature of competition.

331
25:18.122 --> 25:21.625
And if an exciting festival followed to reinforce that…

332
25:23.794 --> 25:25.212
Please put it more simply.

333
25:25.296 --> 25:27.673
We determine the best Korean chef.

334
25:27.757 --> 25:28.758
Not the best in Korea,

335
25:28.841 --> 25:31.010
but the best Korean chef in the world.

336
25:31.093 --> 25:33.637
Not the restaurant with the most Plates.

337
25:33.721 --> 25:36.515
But a person who is judged by top critics at home, abroad

338
25:36.599 --> 25:39.143
and ordinary diners for creating the ultimate dish.

339
25:42.480 --> 25:44.732
We eliminate scores and find a star.

340
25:44.815 --> 25:47.610
That is the competition I'd like us to make.

341
25:48.402 --> 25:50.237
So, the best Korean chef.

342
25:51.947 --> 25:53.240
The best dish.

343
25:53.324 --> 25:55.493
We cast aside the shell that is Plate In Asia,

344
25:55.576 --> 25:57.036
return the essence of cooking

345
25:57.119 --> 26:00.039
and showcase the present and future of K-food.

346
26:00.122 --> 26:01.457
We'll show

347
26:02.416 --> 26:05.378
that this is the path we at Pyeongyeon will take.

348
26:11.133 --> 26:12.885
-And the title? -Sorry?

349
26:14.053 --> 26:15.137
What's the program called?

350
26:17.098 --> 26:20.726
The Table: K-Chef 2026.

351
26:23.771 --> 26:24.980
[Woo-jin] Korea's best chef?

352
26:30.528 --> 26:31.529
Mmm.

353
26:31.612 --> 26:35.658
The working title is The Table: K-Chef 2026.

354
26:40.704 --> 26:41.705
What?

355
26:42.832 --> 26:43.833
You don't like it?

356
26:45.042 --> 26:47.044
It was pretty well-received internally.

357
26:47.962 --> 26:48.963
No.

358
26:49.672 --> 26:50.673
It's not that.

359
26:51.882 --> 26:54.760
I just can't picture what kind of people will compete in this show.

360
26:56.303 --> 26:57.388
Or what it will look like.

361
26:57.471 --> 26:58.722
Like the name says,

362
26:58.806 --> 27:01.642
we gather every single top Korean chef out there.

363
27:01.725 --> 27:06.021
Gosh, I can't wait to see what kind of dishes they'll come up with.

364
27:09.733 --> 27:12.570
You said it starts airing in two months. Is that even possible?

365
27:12.653 --> 27:15.156
The program we were developing had a similar format.

366
27:15.239 --> 27:17.408
So I think we can just give it a different spin.

367
27:18.075 --> 27:19.452
Thank goodness.

368
27:21.078 --> 27:24.331
And plus, the toughest part about a show like this

369
27:24.415 --> 27:29.378
is securing distinguished judges, especially the head judge.

370
27:30.463 --> 27:31.464
Hmm.

371
27:33.174 --> 27:34.717
Guess who we got.

372
27:34.800 --> 27:36.177
Tell me.

373
27:39.138 --> 27:41.474
Henri Bernier. [chuckles]

374
27:43.476 --> 27:45.603
Wow… [laughs]

375
27:46.812 --> 27:47.897
Henri Bernier?

376
27:49.648 --> 27:51.317
You landed a real heavyweight.

377
27:52.026 --> 27:53.903
[chuckles]

378
27:55.362 --> 27:57.531
[Jeong-won] Why don't you want to compete?

379
28:03.329 --> 28:04.413
Bae Yeong-su.

380
28:05.206 --> 28:06.457
Yes, Chef.

381
28:13.005 --> 28:14.715
Did you check the temperature?

382
28:15.257 --> 28:16.467
Uh, yes.

383
28:17.051 --> 28:18.052
Yes, Chef.

384
28:18.135 --> 28:19.428
-Thermometer. -[snaps fingers]

385
28:30.356 --> 28:31.357
What is it?

386
28:36.403 --> 28:37.571
What is it?

387
28:38.405 --> 28:40.032
It's 67°C, Chef.

388
28:40.783 --> 28:43.536
How many times have I told you to get it to 50°C?

389
28:45.287 --> 28:47.456
This is so overcooked, it might as well be burned.

390
28:47.540 --> 28:48.707
[metal clattering]

391
28:48.791 --> 28:51.210
You're a sous-chef and you can't even tell from looking at the color?

392
28:52.044 --> 28:54.255
I'm sorry, Chef. I'm sorry.

393
28:57.174 --> 28:59.677
I forgot and had them arroser it as well.

394
28:59.760 --> 29:01.178
I'm sorry, Chef.

395
29:02.054 --> 29:04.557
Go make it again, and don't forget to check the temperature.

396
29:04.640 --> 29:06.016
Yes, sir.

397
29:06.100 --> 29:08.435
No need, Chef Oh.

398
29:09.770 --> 29:10.813
Michael Jang.

399
29:11.397 --> 29:12.398
Yes, Chef.

400
29:12.940 --> 29:13.941
Finish this.

401
29:17.319 --> 29:18.320
[sighs]

402
29:18.862 --> 29:19.863
You do it.

403
29:20.864 --> 29:21.865
Sorry?

404
29:21.949 --> 29:23.450
[Woo-jin] You cook it.

405
29:23.534 --> 29:24.785
To 50°C.

406
29:31.125 --> 29:32.501
Yes, understood, Chef.

407
29:38.799 --> 29:40.217
-Go and finish up. -Okay.

408
29:59.445 --> 30:01.363
Oh. [sighs]

409
30:01.447 --> 30:02.448
Sorry.

410
30:03.198 --> 30:04.825
What were you saying?

411
30:04.908 --> 30:05.909
Oh.

412
30:07.745 --> 30:09.622
So you're sure you're not going to compete

413
30:10.372 --> 30:12.207
in The Table: 2026?

414
30:13.042 --> 30:14.043
Mmm.

415
30:14.126 --> 30:16.837
Huh? You are?

416
30:16.920 --> 30:18.964
[chuckles] No. I'm not.

417
30:19.048 --> 30:20.466
[sighs] Oh.

418
30:22.009 --> 30:23.010
Why is that?

419
30:23.844 --> 30:26.347
[chuckles] I'm already the best chef in Korea.

420
30:28.140 --> 30:30.267
Why would I enter a competition like that?

421
30:35.022 --> 30:37.483
[chattering]

422
30:37.566 --> 30:39.652
ONE MONTH LATER

423
30:39.735 --> 30:41.278
-Hello. -Hi.

424
30:46.075 --> 30:47.242
1,000 WON EACH

425
30:49.036 --> 30:50.704
Hey, ma'am. I'm gonna taste this, okay?

426
30:54.750 --> 30:55.751
Mmm.

427
30:59.171 --> 31:01.340
Wow, Korean chickens are bigger than I thought.

428
31:19.733 --> 31:21.610
Hey, ma'am, when did these come in?

429
31:30.202 --> 31:32.162
Ma'am, can I get three of these too?

430
32:23.255 --> 32:24.757
FOR THE DECEASED

431
32:56.455 --> 32:58.540
I never thought that photo I took of your father

432
32:58.624 --> 33:01.001
would end up as his funeral portrait.

433
33:03.587 --> 33:04.588
Do you remember?

434
33:05.714 --> 33:06.799
That day.

435
33:07.382 --> 33:09.384
I'd made some homemade makgeolli.

436
33:09.468 --> 33:12.262
Your father and I had some and knocked right out.

437
33:12.346 --> 33:15.849
You must've caught a whiff of what was left and wondered what it was,

438
33:16.725 --> 33:20.521
because then you snuck a few sips and got drunk.

439
33:21.480 --> 33:24.274
Next thing we knew, you were throwing up all over the yard,

440
33:24.358 --> 33:26.193
wailing that your whole body was on fire

441
33:26.276 --> 33:27.486
and that you were going to die.

442
33:28.278 --> 33:30.113
Goodness, we woke up to you screaming,

443
33:30.197 --> 33:33.116
thinking you'd been bitten by a snake while we were asleep.

444
33:33.200 --> 33:37.246
So we stripped you down, searching all over your body for a bite mark.

445
33:37.329 --> 33:38.664
-Then you said… -[chuckles]

446
33:38.747 --> 33:42.626
…"Help me, mister! Mister, the sky is spinning.

447
33:42.709 --> 33:46.129
Mister, the sky is moving. Please!

448
33:46.213 --> 33:47.339
-Help me!" -Yeah, I remember.

449
33:48.549 --> 33:51.385
[sighs] It's been almost 30 years, and I still remember it.

450
33:57.224 --> 34:02.396
[singing in Korean]

451
34:08.318 --> 34:13.156
[singing in Korean]

452
34:24.167 --> 34:25.168
You remember?

453
34:25.961 --> 34:27.796
Well, it was my father's favorite song.

454
34:31.508 --> 34:34.219
[San's friend] I've never seen such an impressive memorial table.

455
34:34.803 --> 34:36.013
Your father would be proud.

456
34:37.222 --> 34:38.515
He'd really be proud of you.

457
34:44.730 --> 34:46.273
Goodness, you old fool.

458
34:46.857 --> 34:48.734
You should've stayed a little longer.

459
34:48.817 --> 34:52.654
You left so soon, you never even got to have a taste of your son's cooking.

460
34:52.738 --> 34:53.655
You're missing out.

461
34:56.366 --> 34:57.367
Han.

462
34:59.161 --> 35:00.412
Yes, sir?

463
35:01.455 --> 35:03.749
I remember

464
35:03.832 --> 35:05.626
when you came back here, two years ago…

465
35:07.920 --> 35:11.798
you had questions written all over your face.

466
35:13.342 --> 35:17.220
So, have you found the answers to those questions?

467
35:19.306 --> 35:21.475
You said you wanted to find yourself.

468
35:23.268 --> 35:24.311
Well, did you?

469
35:25.562 --> 35:26.939
Did you find yourself?

470
35:38.450 --> 35:41.870
[singing in Korean]

471
35:53.715 --> 35:54.716
Han.

472
35:58.220 --> 36:00.764
Today, I'm missing your father even more.

473
36:20.242 --> 36:23.453
Come on. Please. Could you reconsider just one more time?

474
36:23.537 --> 36:26.581
We haven't had any sales whatsoever for a month now.

475
36:26.665 --> 36:30.168
What good is having a fancy restaurant when we aren't making any money, huh?

476
36:30.252 --> 36:34.965
I'm so sorry, but you don't meet the eligibility requirements.

477
36:35.048 --> 36:37.300
Uh, you've been registered as a co-owner

478
36:37.384 --> 36:39.511
with your late father for the past four years,

479
36:39.594 --> 36:41.596
so you don't qualify.

480
36:41.680 --> 36:46.226
I'm telling you, you might have better luck with a small-business loan instead.

481
36:47.352 --> 36:49.021
SMALL-BUSINESS LOAN COUNTER

482
36:49.104 --> 36:51.481
Uh, unfortunately, you're too late.

483
36:52.149 --> 36:54.359
Applications for this quarter closed last week.

484
36:55.360 --> 36:57.237
[sighs]

485
37:00.574 --> 37:01.575
Yes, hello.

486
37:01.658 --> 37:04.119
I'm sorry to bother you. It's me calling you again.

487
37:04.202 --> 37:07.664
I wired you two million won toward what we owe you.

488
37:08.582 --> 37:12.711
Do you think it would be possible to give me another month to pay you the rest?

489
37:13.837 --> 37:15.422
I'd really appreciate it.

490
37:15.505 --> 37:19.217
I want to pay you as soon as possible, but things at Famiglia are…

491
37:21.386 --> 37:24.473
Yes, thank you. I'll wire you the rest as soon as I can.

492
37:24.556 --> 37:26.016
All right. Thank you.

493
37:29.895 --> 37:31.521
[sighs deeply]

494
38:03.595 --> 38:04.805
Oh, hello.

495
38:06.098 --> 38:07.432
When did you get here?

496
38:08.308 --> 38:09.309
Ms. Choi.

497
38:09.392 --> 38:12.104
I managed to persuade Chef Cho Deok-rae.

498
38:13.396 --> 38:16.983
He thought it over, and he agreed to testify that Pyeongyeon threatened him.

499
38:17.067 --> 38:18.610
Did he really?

500
38:18.693 --> 38:19.694
Yes.

501
38:19.778 --> 38:23.907
If we can get just one more witness, I think we'll have a real chance.

502
38:24.491 --> 38:26.451
Ideally, someone who used to work here.

503
38:27.536 --> 38:28.870
That is such a relief.

504
38:28.954 --> 38:30.622
Seriously, it really is.

505
38:31.123 --> 38:32.874
I don't know how to pay you, sir.

506
38:32.958 --> 38:35.377
Thank you. Thank you so, so, so much.

507
38:36.086 --> 38:41.591
Uh, of course, finding someone willing to testify won't be that easy.

508
38:41.675 --> 38:42.968
But still,

509
38:43.051 --> 38:46.388
I hope we'll be able to find someone.

510
38:48.223 --> 38:50.851
[sighs] Someone who used to work here, huh?

511
38:52.435 --> 38:54.229
Um… Ms. Choi.

512
38:56.273 --> 38:57.274
Actually,

513
38:57.941 --> 39:01.570
I got a call just this morning. They said they wanted to meet.

514
39:04.197 --> 39:05.198
A call from who?

515
39:09.911 --> 39:10.912
Was it…

516
39:13.623 --> 39:14.749
Was it Pyeongyeon?

517
39:16.334 --> 39:18.712
"I have no intention of dropping the lawsuit.

518
39:18.795 --> 39:21.506
Whatever terms you offer, I'm not interested," huh?

519
39:26.011 --> 39:27.762
What does she want then?

520
39:28.346 --> 39:31.224
She can't be rejecting everything. There must be something she wants.

521
39:35.645 --> 39:36.938
[knocking on table]

522
39:39.191 --> 39:40.442
Ms. Baek Hyeon-ju?

523
39:45.155 --> 39:47.490
Well, uh, the thing is…

524
39:48.533 --> 39:51.203
that she didn't really seem to want anything.

525
39:51.286 --> 39:54.664
She just went on about her father's honor or something like that…

526
39:56.416 --> 39:59.878
But accepting our offer is the way to restore Chef Choi Seung-Hyo's name.

527
39:59.961 --> 40:02.547
It'll save the restaurant's reputation too. Don't you agree?

528
40:03.131 --> 40:06.343
Well, that is true, but… [inhales]

529
40:06.426 --> 40:08.094
…from the way she reacted,

530
40:08.178 --> 40:11.139
I don't think that's all she wants, you know what I mean?

531
40:14.476 --> 40:17.979
She said that she'd sue Pyeongyeon and uncover the truth.

532
40:19.147 --> 40:22.192
She kept going on about that, which isn't even realistically possible.

533
40:22.275 --> 40:24.611
And, uh, it's driving me up the wall.

534
40:25.862 --> 40:30.951
[sighs] And just when things were getting complicated, a few of those bastards

535
40:31.451 --> 40:35.372
who are now suddenly coming forward, saying we threatened them into lying.

536
40:35.872 --> 40:40.710
Really. They're apparently going to testify or something.

537
40:46.216 --> 40:47.509
She wants to start a lawsuit

538
40:47.592 --> 40:50.220
and see it through to the end, no matter if it takes one year or ten?

539
40:51.137 --> 40:52.138
Against Pyeongyeon?

540
40:52.222 --> 40:53.640
Yes!

541
40:54.182 --> 40:55.684
She's insane!

542
40:56.184 --> 40:59.020
I'm telling you, she's nuts. A total nutcase.

543
40:59.104 --> 41:00.689
[Song-yi] That's right. I am.

544
41:01.189 --> 41:04.359
A nutcase.

545
41:07.362 --> 41:08.697
But that's too bad.

546
41:09.698 --> 41:11.533
I hear there's no cure for being a nutcase.

547
41:11.616 --> 41:13.410
Why, you little…

548
41:16.871 --> 41:18.748
[whimsical music playing]

549
41:24.587 --> 41:25.588
[clears throat]

550
41:27.716 --> 41:29.050
[sighs]

551
41:30.719 --> 41:32.178
She doesn't want money.

552
41:32.262 --> 41:35.682
She's not interested in Pyeongyeon's offer to restore Famiglia's reputation either.

553
41:35.765 --> 41:38.601
Win or lose, she's going to fight to the end.

554
41:39.102 --> 41:40.645
She wants to tell the world that

555
41:40.729 --> 41:43.648
her father was driven to his death by Pyeongyeon Group's

556
41:45.483 --> 41:47.193
manipulation and threats.

557
41:47.986 --> 41:49.195
[sighs]

558
41:53.074 --> 41:55.535
The more complicated you make things, the more leaks you create.

559
41:57.829 --> 42:00.707
Editing recordings, threatening those involved,

560
42:00.790 --> 42:02.125
inducing false statements,

561
42:02.208 --> 42:05.086
bribery and manipulating public opinion through paid commentors.

562
42:06.171 --> 42:10.800
Did you really think this old playbook would work in this day and age? Really?

563
42:11.843 --> 42:13.261
Ms. Baek Chun-ja.

564
42:19.017 --> 42:21.186
[Hae-seon] The competition is only a month away.

565
42:21.269 --> 42:24.856
It's the project we're betting everything on to contain the Famiglia crisis.

566
42:24.939 --> 42:28.568
We're giving up on Plate In Asia to find the best Korean chef.

567
42:29.277 --> 42:31.946
Tell me, little sister, what would it look like

568
42:32.989 --> 42:36.534
if we were sued by Famiglia while hosting such a prestigious competition?

569
42:37.827 --> 42:39.120
If people out there hear that

570
42:39.204 --> 42:42.457
Pyeongyeon Group drove a respected chef to his premature death,

571
42:43.041 --> 42:46.086
do you think they'll want to watch a competition we put on?

572
42:47.212 --> 42:48.213
Huh?

573
42:50.048 --> 42:51.132
Chun-ja.

574
42:54.844 --> 42:57.430
[grunting]

575
42:57.514 --> 43:01.684
I could wring that woman's damn neck! What an insufferable bitch!

576
43:04.938 --> 43:07.399
[grunting, shouts]

577
43:07.482 --> 43:08.525
[screams]

578
43:09.734 --> 43:13.279
She tosses me a CEO position at some lousy cable station

579
43:13.363 --> 43:15.865
and keeps calling me by my old name.

580
43:15.949 --> 43:17.826
"Hey, Ms. Baek Chun-ja."

581
43:17.909 --> 43:19.327
Oh. Damn it.

582
43:19.411 --> 43:21.413
Ms. Baek Chun-ja! Damn it!

583
43:21.496 --> 43:22.872
[grunts]

584
43:22.956 --> 43:26.042
Did I do all of that for own my sake? Huh?

585
43:26.126 --> 43:27.544
It was all for the company.

586
43:27.627 --> 43:31.965
The company! The company! The company! The company! [shouts]

587
43:32.799 --> 43:34.592
[groaning quietly]

588
43:36.428 --> 43:37.429
What?

589
43:37.512 --> 43:38.721
Did that hurt?

590
43:40.807 --> 43:42.392
[groans] I'm fine.

591
43:42.475 --> 43:45.270
This is nothing. [pants] Piece of cake.

592
43:45.353 --> 43:48.106
Right, you're fine. This is nothing.

593
43:48.731 --> 43:49.816
Get that away!

594
43:51.860 --> 43:52.861
"This is nothing"?

595
43:53.820 --> 43:55.280
[laughs] "This is nothing"?

596
43:56.406 --> 43:57.615
"This is nothing"?

597
43:58.116 --> 44:00.952
Hey. Are you looking down on me too?

598
44:01.035 --> 44:02.620
-Huh? -Huh?

599
44:03.580 --> 44:04.706
Huh?

600
44:04.789 --> 44:06.541
-No, ma'am. -Just because

601
44:06.624 --> 44:10.044
I was born out of wedlock and brought into the family,

602
44:10.128 --> 44:12.964
are you looking down on me too?

603
44:13.047 --> 44:13.965
No, ma'am.

604
44:14.048 --> 44:15.508
[yelling]

605
44:15.592 --> 44:17.177
No. That's not it.

606
44:17.260 --> 44:18.428
I'm sorry. I was wrong.

607
44:18.511 --> 44:19.971
I'm sorry.

608
44:20.054 --> 44:22.015
I really didn't mean it that way. I'm sorry.

609
44:23.057 --> 44:24.058
Open it.

610
44:26.352 --> 44:27.687
What the… [splutters]

611
44:27.770 --> 44:30.190
Why is she sending me emails in the middle of the night?

612
44:30.773 --> 44:34.402
Still, it's about the head judge, so I should take a look.

613
44:34.486 --> 44:35.487
Let's see.

614
44:35.570 --> 44:36.946
GOURMET COLUMNIST, AUTHOR, CULINARY COMPETITION JUDGE

615
44:37.030 --> 44:38.364
This is all stuff I already know.

616
44:38.448 --> 44:39.365
Next page.

617
44:39.991 --> 44:43.119
EXPERTISE

618
44:43.203 --> 44:44.204
Next.

619
44:46.748 --> 44:47.749
Next.

620
44:49.876 --> 44:51.794
FAMILY

621
44:51.878 --> 44:53.922
DESIGNER, MOVED TO PARIS IN 1963 TO STUDY

622
44:54.005 --> 44:55.882
Oh!

623
44:55.965 --> 44:58.009
So his mother is Korean?

624
44:58.092 --> 44:59.886
So that's why he speaks some Korean.

625
45:00.720 --> 45:01.971
Next.

626
45:02.055 --> 45:03.765
3 MISTELLA STARS FOR 13 CONSECUTIVE YEARS

627
45:03.848 --> 45:05.183
Wow!

628
45:06.142 --> 45:07.769
Beautiful. Beautiful.

629
45:08.394 --> 45:10.021
Fantastic.

630
45:10.104 --> 45:11.606
This is really impressive.

631
45:11.689 --> 45:13.650
Wow!

632
45:13.733 --> 45:16.778
No wonder Ms. Seon was desperate to lock him down for the show.

633
45:16.861 --> 45:18.905
Wow!

634
45:20.240 --> 45:22.325
What time is his plane landing tomorrow?

635
45:23.993 --> 45:26.913
Henri Bernier! I'm talking about Henri Bernier!

636
45:26.996 --> 45:28.581
His plane lands at…

637
45:28.665 --> 45:29.791
At? At? At? At?

638
45:29.874 --> 45:32.377
Oh. His plane lands at 4:15 p.m.

639
45:32.460 --> 45:34.379
Have my car ready on time.

640
45:35.713 --> 45:37.340
You're going to the airport to greet him yourself?

641
45:37.423 --> 45:39.425
Why? Can't I go?

642
45:39.509 --> 45:42.345
Well, Ms. Seon is going to the airport to…

643
45:42.428 --> 45:43.596
Hyeong-koo.

644
45:44.347 --> 45:46.683
-Hyeong-koo. -Yes?

645
45:47.559 --> 45:49.561
We're bringing in such a distinguished figure

646
45:49.644 --> 45:54.274
as the head judge for such an important competition like this.

647
45:54.857 --> 45:58.111
And you think it's okay to send a team leader to pick him up?

648
45:58.194 --> 46:00.321
You absolute airhead. Why? Why, you airhead?

649
46:00.405 --> 46:02.031
Yes. You're… You're right.

650
46:02.115 --> 46:03.366
-Smile. -Ah.

651
46:05.577 --> 46:06.869
[Hyeon-ju chuckling]

652
46:09.831 --> 46:12.375
Personally, rather than this circular design,

653
46:12.458 --> 46:15.503
I think this layout looks much simpler and cleaner.

654
46:16.588 --> 46:17.589
If you look here,

655
46:17.672 --> 46:20.383
having them run through the corridor into the pantry

656
46:20.466 --> 46:22.719
could make for a really fun sequence.

657
46:22.802 --> 46:25.179
Could we widen the hallway just a little bit?

658
46:25.263 --> 46:27.390
-I think we can do that. -[knocking on door]

659
46:32.395 --> 46:33.396
[producer] Chairwoman.

660
46:36.816 --> 46:39.360
Well, the concept looks pretty good like this.

661
46:40.737 --> 46:42.905
When the chefs split off into their kitchens,

662
46:42.989 --> 46:46.951
will the screens up here show what's happening in each kitchen?

663
46:47.035 --> 46:48.536
-Yes, that's right. -Mmm.

664
46:50.413 --> 46:52.332
So this is the judges' table, right?

665
46:52.415 --> 46:54.500
That's where the main judges will sit.

666
46:54.584 --> 46:56.461
And the one in the middle is Henri Bernier's?

667
46:56.544 --> 46:58.129
Mm-hmm. Yes.

668
46:58.212 --> 46:59.797
He's arriving today, right?

669
46:59.881 --> 47:01.007
Yes.

670
47:01.090 --> 47:04.344
Ms. Baek is personally going to the airport to greet him in two hours.

671
47:04.427 --> 47:06.679
I'll be accompanying her there.

672
47:06.763 --> 47:10.391
[scoffs] Of course she wants to insert herself wherever she can be seen.

673
47:10.475 --> 47:12.143
Good grief.

674
47:13.311 --> 47:16.105
What about Cha Woo-jin? Is he still refusing to compete?

675
47:20.985 --> 47:23.112
We're trying to find Korea's best chef.

676
47:23.196 --> 47:25.615
It wouldn't look right if Exception didn't compete.

677
47:26.324 --> 47:28.242
[chuckles] I agree with you, ma'am.

678
47:28.826 --> 47:31.287
The standard approach won't work on someone like him.

679
47:31.371 --> 47:34.165
Skip the talk about meaning or purpose of the competition.

680
47:34.999 --> 47:38.753
Find a more direct way to appeal to his innermost emotions.

681
47:39.587 --> 47:40.838
Yes, Chairwoman.

682
47:41.881 --> 47:43.383
[upbeat music playing]

683
47:58.356 --> 47:59.607
Thank you.

684
48:12.328 --> 48:13.830
-[sighs] -[elevator bell dings]

685
48:17.291 --> 48:19.210
Please, Chef. I'm begging you.

686
48:19.293 --> 48:21.254
All you have to do is tell the truth.

687
48:21.337 --> 48:23.423
Don't do this. You're making things harder.

688
48:23.506 --> 48:24.966
Can't you just drop this now?

689
48:25.049 --> 48:27.552
I'm not asking for anything else, I promise.

690
48:27.635 --> 48:31.222
Just do this one thing for my late father's sake and I'll leave you alone.

691
48:31.305 --> 48:32.306
Please?

692
48:32.390 --> 48:33.474
[sighs]

693
48:34.183 --> 48:37.854
Eight years. That's how long you and Dad worked together.

694
48:38.354 --> 48:41.691
You know how much my dad appreciated and cared about you.

695
48:42.358 --> 48:45.069
Please just testify about the verbal abuse and sexual harassment,

696
48:45.153 --> 48:46.154
that none of it is true.

697
48:46.237 --> 48:49.782
You know he wasn't like that. Do it for his memory, please.

698
48:53.578 --> 48:55.830
Do you really think they'll stop once they destroy us?

699
48:57.331 --> 48:59.500
You know they won't.

700
48:59.584 --> 49:01.127
If you don't do as they say,

701
49:02.086 --> 49:05.465
Pyeongyeon Group will destroy you the same way they destroyed us some day.

702
49:08.634 --> 49:10.011
I'm sorry, Song-yi.

703
49:10.094 --> 49:12.346
Oh, Chef. Chef…

704
49:12.430 --> 49:14.515
-Please, please… -Will you stop, Song-yi?

705
49:17.727 --> 49:19.020
[Song-yi sniffles]

706
49:19.103 --> 49:20.563
Song-yi, don't try too hard.

707
49:23.357 --> 49:26.444
Some things can't be changed.

708
49:28.321 --> 49:29.447
[sighs]

709
49:34.494 --> 49:35.661
[sniffles]

710
49:54.222 --> 49:56.057
[gasping]

711
49:56.808 --> 49:57.767
Are you okay?

712
49:59.602 --> 50:00.603
Thank you.

713
50:02.021 --> 50:03.022
[sniffles]

714
50:18.246 --> 50:20.206
[sighs, clicks tongue]

715
50:21.749 --> 50:22.917
[sighs]

716
50:24.085 --> 50:26.170
[door opening]

717
50:27.547 --> 50:29.632
Why haven't you been answering your phone?

718
50:30.424 --> 50:33.970
Oh, I'm sorry. I had it on silent.

719
50:35.263 --> 50:36.430
[sighs]

720
50:37.223 --> 50:38.641
What's wrong, Auntie?

721
50:39.350 --> 50:40.893
Did something happen?

722
50:42.937 --> 50:44.814
Mr. Park called while you were out.

723
50:45.898 --> 50:48.901
He says he can't keep supplying us with ingredients on credit.

724
50:48.985 --> 50:50.778
He's cutting us off starting with tonight's service.

725
50:50.862 --> 50:51.863
What?

726
50:52.864 --> 50:54.907
Then how are we supposed to open tonight?

727
50:54.991 --> 50:56.117
[sighs]

728
50:56.909 --> 50:58.244
Oh, this is bad.

729
50:59.245 --> 51:01.372
Um, I'll go talk to the chef de partie right away.

730
51:01.455 --> 51:06.168
Don't bother. The chef de partie quit. He packed up and left two hours ago.

731
51:06.252 --> 51:08.004
What? Why?

732
51:08.087 --> 51:09.422
I don't know. [sighs]

733
51:09.505 --> 51:12.758
I tried talking to him, but he just quit.

734
51:13.843 --> 51:16.095
He isn't getting paid, and now with no ingredients…

735
51:16.178 --> 51:18.014
[sighs] How could he not quit?

736
51:23.519 --> 51:25.646
-What should we do, Auntie? -[sighs]

737
51:25.730 --> 51:27.023
Tonight's dinner service…

738
51:27.106 --> 51:29.609
What do you mean, what should we do? We have to close.

739
51:30.526 --> 51:32.820
We have no ingredients, no staff,

740
51:33.821 --> 51:35.448
and we have no customers.

741
51:39.285 --> 51:40.286
Song-yi,

742
51:40.995 --> 51:42.163
you know,

743
51:42.872 --> 51:46.500
maybe… maybe we should close for a while.

744
51:46.584 --> 51:48.920
Nobody is applying, so what can the two of us possibly do?

745
51:49.962 --> 51:51.297
And…

746
51:52.882 --> 51:55.217
you and I, we are both…

747
51:56.969 --> 51:58.054
exhausted.

748
51:58.137 --> 51:59.555
[whimpers]

749
52:05.269 --> 52:09.440
[sniffles] No matter how hard things got, we've managed to tough it out this far.

750
52:14.779 --> 52:16.405
I promised I would…

751
52:21.452 --> 52:24.288
I promised I would protect it until the very end.

752
52:27.333 --> 52:29.001
[sighs]

753
52:33.214 --> 52:35.967
[Song-yi] No. We can't keep doing this.

754
52:38.386 --> 52:40.846
We've done well just to hold on this long.

755
52:42.390 --> 52:43.641
Everyone

756
52:44.767 --> 52:46.477
will understand that I tried.

757
52:47.311 --> 52:48.312
Even Dad.

758
52:52.817 --> 52:54.068
Oh, Dad…

759
53:00.741 --> 53:03.452
[Song-yi] This is exactly what they want.

760
53:03.536 --> 53:06.163
For Famiglia to shut down and disappear.

761
53:07.164 --> 53:09.792
To erase my Dad's memory from this world.

762
53:12.461 --> 53:14.213
If I give up on Famiglia

763
53:16.090 --> 53:18.134
just because things are really hard…

764
53:23.055 --> 53:24.682
[sniffles]

765
53:25.766 --> 53:26.851
Where are you going?

766
53:26.934 --> 53:30.479
I'll go talk to Mr. Park. I'll ask him to give us just a few more days.

767
53:31.105 --> 53:33.149
Oh, and I'll meet with the chef de partie

768
53:33.232 --> 53:36.110
and try to persuade him to stay until the end of the month.

769
53:36.193 --> 53:39.613
Anyway, I'll go get what we need, whether it's ingredients or people.

770
53:41.699 --> 53:42.783
[sighs]

771
53:51.125 --> 53:53.711
[whirring]

772
53:59.300 --> 54:00.301
What the…

773
54:06.390 --> 54:08.059
Is the cooling fan broken?

774
54:13.522 --> 54:14.940
Huh?

775
54:15.024 --> 54:16.358
I don't think it is.

776
54:18.235 --> 54:20.071
Well, that's just odd.

777
54:29.205 --> 54:30.289
[sighs]

778
54:34.085 --> 54:35.795
[phone buzzes]

779
54:38.172 --> 54:39.215
[chuckles]

780
54:42.510 --> 54:43.594
Hey, Sarah.

781
54:43.677 --> 54:45.346
[Sarah] Everything okay?

782
54:45.429 --> 54:46.430
Yep.

783
54:46.514 --> 54:49.141
We're all longing to see you, Chris.

784
54:50.017 --> 54:54.522
I hate to say this, but if you don't keep your promise again,

785
54:55.231 --> 54:57.733
the manager is going to sue you.

786
54:58.692 --> 55:00.194
So please,

787
55:00.277 --> 55:02.863
tell me you're leaving Korea tomorrow as scheduled.

788
55:04.073 --> 55:05.199
Don't worry, Sarah.

789
55:05.282 --> 55:08.661
12:45 p.m., tomorrow, Incheon Airport.

790
55:09.245 --> 55:10.871
I'll be there for sure this time.

791
55:11.705 --> 55:13.374
[chuckles] Okay. Thank God.

792
55:13.874 --> 55:17.044
I can't believe I'm finally going to see you again in New York.

793
55:21.090 --> 55:22.216
I miss New York.

794
55:23.259 --> 55:24.760
I miss you guys.

795
55:24.844 --> 55:26.053
And you too, Sarah.

796
55:26.137 --> 55:27.638
I miss you all.

797
55:27.721 --> 55:29.765
We all really miss you, Chris.

798
55:30.641 --> 55:32.059
And your food.

799
55:32.143 --> 55:35.312
Our customers are dying to eat your dish again,

800
55:35.396 --> 55:39.400
and I'm so excited to see what you're going to show us after the past two years.

801
55:39.900 --> 55:41.277
I wish you a safe trip.

802
55:41.360 --> 55:42.736
See you soon.

803
55:42.820 --> 55:44.196
Yep. See you soon.

804
55:45.781 --> 55:46.824
[phone beeps]

805
55:54.748 --> 55:56.959
[gentle music playing]

806
56:07.761 --> 56:10.264
[San] Cooking isn't science or technique.

807
56:10.347 --> 56:11.348
It's about heart.

808
56:25.321 --> 56:28.115
It's about cooking with just one person in mind,

809
56:28.199 --> 56:29.992
the person who will eat your food.

810
56:40.127 --> 56:42.713
[sighs, chuckles]

811
56:42.796 --> 56:46.217
It's about truly moving that person with your sincerity.

812
57:04.318 --> 57:06.403
That's what real cooking is.

813
57:06.487 --> 57:09.365
Just like the food we're having today.

814
57:12.326 --> 57:13.410
[chuckles]

815
57:14.745 --> 57:16.705
Oh, Chef Choi. Over here.

816
57:23.712 --> 57:24.713
Hey.

817
57:26.924 --> 57:28.634
This is my son, Han.

818
57:30.261 --> 57:31.679
Han, say hello.

819
57:31.762 --> 57:33.764
He is the chef here at Famiglia.

820
57:52.866 --> 57:53.951
[chuckles quietly]

821
58:00.624 --> 58:02.084
I'll have the signature course.

822
58:02.167 --> 58:03.919
Okay. Of course.

823
58:15.556 --> 58:18.100
[Han] She didn't even ask about the wine.

824
58:18.976 --> 58:21.895
It's early, but still, not a single customer.

825
58:23.105 --> 58:25.399
It's the place I came to years ago.

826
58:25.482 --> 58:27.443
Things haven't changed so much.

827
58:29.486 --> 58:30.654
So…

828
58:31.572 --> 58:33.449
what is this chill in the air?

829
58:35.659 --> 58:38.245
I feel that raw odor of freshly…

830
58:39.621 --> 58:40.873
thawed meat.

831
58:45.878 --> 58:47.421
What are you talking about?

832
58:48.630 --> 58:50.090
Chef Choi Seung-hyo is dead?

833
58:50.174 --> 58:51.175
Well…

834
58:52.426 --> 58:54.345
It's quite unfortunate. I'm sorry.

835
58:57.014 --> 59:01.643
I was really looking forward to… eating at Famiglia again.

836
59:02.853 --> 59:04.605
[Hyeon-ju] Don't be too disappointed.

837
59:04.688 --> 59:07.441
Ms. Seon here has reserved the…

838
59:07.524 --> 59:09.943
best restaurant in the country to welcome you to Korea.

839
59:10.027 --> 59:12.488
You know Exception, don't you?

840
59:12.571 --> 59:14.615
Chef Cha Woo-jin's Exception.

841
59:15.282 --> 59:18.577
We've asked Chef Cha to put extra care into your meal,

842
59:18.660 --> 59:22.122
so you're in for a very special experience tonight.

843
59:22.831 --> 59:23.999
Right, Ms. Seon?

844
59:24.083 --> 59:26.251
[chuckles] Yes.

845
59:28.796 --> 59:30.923
ANTIPASTO - SEARED SCALLOPS WITH VONGOLE SAUCE

846
01:00:02.871 --> 01:00:04.456
[swallows loudly]

847
01:00:04.540 --> 01:00:05.624
How is it?

848
01:00:07.000 --> 01:00:10.045
It's fresh scallops seared quickly over high heat

849
01:00:10.129 --> 01:00:13.006
and topped with a classic clam sauce.

850
01:00:13.090 --> 01:00:14.091
Delicious.

851
01:00:23.851 --> 01:00:26.520
SHRIMP RAVIOLI

852
01:00:37.114 --> 01:00:38.365
[San] Is it good, Son?

853
01:00:39.408 --> 01:00:42.494
It's the best. It's so good, Dad. [chuckles]

854
01:00:43.662 --> 01:00:45.038
[coughing]

855
01:00:53.130 --> 01:00:54.256
[sighs]

856
01:00:55.507 --> 01:00:56.800
They've gone bad.

857
01:01:05.851 --> 01:01:06.935
Oh, no.

858
01:01:08.479 --> 01:01:09.938
I'm sorry.

859
01:01:10.022 --> 01:01:11.940
We've been using this for a while now.

860
01:01:20.616 --> 01:01:23.327
SPINACH RISOTTO

861
01:01:26.788 --> 01:01:29.041
When you scoop it with the back of a spoon,

862
01:01:29.124 --> 01:01:31.043
it should gently flow back down.

863
01:01:31.543 --> 01:01:35.047
That's the perfect texture for a risotto, Son.

864
01:01:43.889 --> 01:01:44.932
[scoffs]

865
01:01:48.852 --> 01:01:50.646
[Han] The perfect risotto?

866
01:01:54.691 --> 01:01:57.819
MAIN DISH BLACK GOAT SIRLOIN STEAK

867
01:02:02.783 --> 01:02:05.077
[San] Ah, look at this pinkish color.

868
01:02:05.869 --> 01:02:07.496
Won't you eat, Han?

869
01:02:08.497 --> 01:02:11.667
Han, why won't you eat something this delicious?

870
01:02:11.750 --> 01:02:13.835
This is what real cooking is.

871
01:02:14.419 --> 01:02:17.089
Food that moves the diner's heart.

872
01:02:18.423 --> 01:02:20.968
[Han] Smelly scallops and spoiled ravioli.

873
01:02:21.802 --> 01:02:24.263
A perfectly clumpy risotto.

874
01:02:26.098 --> 01:02:28.392
And even a completely dried-out main dish.

875
01:02:28.976 --> 01:02:34.231
I hope you will remember this moment for the rest of your life, Han.

876
01:02:34.856 --> 01:02:35.857
[chuckles]

877
01:02:36.900 --> 01:02:39.111
[Han] Remember for the rest of my life?

878
01:02:39.194 --> 01:02:40.821
[scoffs]

879
01:02:50.914 --> 01:02:52.583
Please take me to Famiglia.

880
01:02:55.502 --> 01:02:59.047
Oh… [stammers] But what do you mean, Monsieur Bernier?

881
01:02:59.798 --> 01:03:02.509
Even though Chef Choi Seung-hyo isn't there anymore?

882
01:03:05.804 --> 01:03:07.806
Uh, yes?

883
01:03:09.308 --> 01:03:10.559
Huh?

884
01:03:11.184 --> 01:03:15.230
[Henri] If Famiglia is still running even after Chef Choi passed away,

885
01:03:15.314 --> 01:03:18.066
that means his staff must be maintaining his tradition

886
01:03:18.734 --> 01:03:21.069
and serving his food the way he would.

887
01:03:26.116 --> 01:03:27.659
I really want to eat

888
01:03:27.743 --> 01:03:29.703
at Famiglia one last time

889
01:03:30.579 --> 01:03:32.748
and remember Chef Choi's food.

890
01:03:35.917 --> 01:03:37.461
[Han] This is a nightmare.

891
01:03:37.544 --> 01:03:38.629
Sorry?

892
01:03:38.712 --> 01:03:42.382
Cooking isn't simply about serving delicious food.

893
01:03:43.342 --> 01:03:45.927
It can bring back someone's precious memories, and even…

894
01:03:46.720 --> 01:03:49.306
give them the courage to keep going in their lives.

895
01:03:50.307 --> 01:03:51.475
But tonight,

896
01:03:52.476 --> 01:03:55.604
you turned a memory from 26 years ago…

897
01:03:55.687 --> 01:03:57.105
into a nightmare.

898
01:03:59.816 --> 01:04:00.901
[scoffs]

899
01:04:06.490 --> 01:04:08.825
Even the most basic cleanup hasn't been done.

900
01:04:10.994 --> 01:04:13.538
[blows] The hygiene is appalling too.

901
01:04:15.874 --> 01:04:18.794
And the staff prepping the signature course? Just one.

902
01:04:20.295 --> 01:04:21.421
You're what?

903
01:04:21.505 --> 01:04:23.548
The sous-chef? The chef de partie?

904
01:04:25.509 --> 01:04:28.595
You serve such dismal food, and the head chef is nowhere to be found?

905
01:04:30.222 --> 01:04:33.266
The quality of the ingredients and the seasoning,

906
01:04:33.350 --> 01:04:36.311
the inconsistent sauces, purees and overcooked meat!

907
01:04:38.689 --> 01:04:40.399
That course was a total disaster.

908
01:04:44.319 --> 01:04:45.946
How did this place end up like this?

909
01:04:48.198 --> 01:04:50.075
Did he let the money and fame

910
01:04:50.784 --> 01:04:52.160
get to his head?

911
01:04:54.830 --> 01:04:57.207
Aren't you the slightest bit ashamed

912
01:04:57.290 --> 01:05:01.044
to serve food like that and disgrace the Famiglia name?

913
01:05:02.170 --> 01:05:03.588
[Song-yi] Watch what you say!

914
01:05:06.717 --> 01:05:09.177
My dad never, not even once,

915
01:05:10.220 --> 01:05:12.431
let anything get to his head.

916
01:05:15.142 --> 01:05:17.644
And that's exactly why he died such an unjust death!

917
01:05:19.187 --> 01:05:21.106
[Han] What is she saying?

918
01:05:21.189 --> 01:05:22.190
"Dad"?

919
01:05:33.076 --> 01:05:34.911
I don't care about any of that.

920
01:05:36.413 --> 01:05:37.998
I'm a customer here.

921
01:05:38.081 --> 01:05:40.709
I came here to eat Famiglia's food.

922
01:05:40.792 --> 01:05:43.920
I don't care if the kitchen's a mess, if the ingredients aren't even prepared

923
01:05:44.004 --> 01:05:45.672
or how bad the service is!

924
01:05:46.423 --> 01:05:50.010
Even if the head chef is away, appearing on some TV show,

925
01:05:51.011 --> 01:05:55.098
this place should've served Famiglia's signature dishes to perfection.

926
01:05:56.892 --> 01:05:59.269
This place isn't even worthy of its name!

927
01:06:00.896 --> 01:06:04.232
[screaming, crying]

928
01:06:04.316 --> 01:06:07.277
-Oh, Song-yi. Song-yi, you okay? -Oh, Auntie…

929
01:06:07.360 --> 01:06:09.529
-[Du-yeong] Hey. -[sobbing continues]

930
01:06:11.448 --> 01:06:12.449
Oh, Auntie…

931
01:06:20.999 --> 01:06:23.460
[crying continues]

932
01:06:25.670 --> 01:06:27.380
[whirring]

933
01:06:30.091 --> 01:06:31.384
[Song-yi] Dad…

934
01:06:31.468 --> 01:06:32.803
[crashing]

935
01:06:37.432 --> 01:06:38.433
Dad…

936
01:06:49.361 --> 01:06:50.695
[whirring continues]

937
01:07:11.091 --> 01:07:12.217
[hissing]

938
01:07:12.843 --> 01:07:13.844
Get down.

939
01:07:18.223 --> 01:07:19.224
I said get down.

940
01:07:19.307 --> 01:07:20.267
What?

941
01:07:26.022 --> 01:07:27.357
Get down!

942
01:07:40.745 --> 01:07:43.290
[mid-tempo music playing]

943
01:07:58.722 --> 01:08:00.515
[pop song playing]

944
01:08:48.563 --> 01:08:52.484
[Du-yeong] Um, by the way, what is it that you do exactly? [gasps]

945
01:08:52.567 --> 01:08:55.153
-[Henri] It's been ten years. -Henri Bernier?

946
01:08:55.236 --> 01:08:56.696
I'd like you to serve dinner tonight.

947
01:08:59.574 --> 01:09:01.201
-Go. -Wow. What is this?

948
01:09:01.284 --> 01:09:02.535
It's perfect.

949
01:09:02.619 --> 01:09:04.663
Find out who he is, and do it quickly.

950
01:09:04.746 --> 01:09:07.040
What his connection to Famiglia is.

951
01:09:07.123 --> 01:09:08.583
[Han] The best K-chef, huh?

952
01:09:10.710 --> 01:09:12.170
The man from yesterday.

953
01:09:12.253 --> 01:09:14.130
We're offering you a deal right now, Ms. Choi.

954
01:09:14.214 --> 01:09:16.508
[Song-yi] I want to show them even if it's just once…

955
01:09:16.591 --> 01:09:19.803
-Dad, please! -…that they can't always have their way.

956
01:09:19.886 --> 01:09:21.054
Please help me.
